                            <name>MSK</name>
                            <description>Self Address Mask for 9-Bit Mode  This field contains the address mask that creates a set of addresses that should be matched.  A 0 bit in the MSK bitfield configures, that the corresponding bit in the ADDR bitfield of the UARTxADDR register is don't care. A 1 bit in the MSK bitfield configures, that the corresponding bit in the ADDR bitfield of the UARTxADDR register must match.</description>
                            <bitOffset>0x0</bitOffset>
                            <bitWidth>0x8</bitWidth>
                            <access>read-write</access>
                            </field>
                    </fields>
